# Source manifest — reproducible-by-reference (Invariant 3).
# Re-clone at build time; the working tree under sources/graphify/ is gitignored.
#
#   git clone --depth 1 --branch <ref> <url> sources/graphify
#   git -C sources/graphify checkout <commit>
#
# First corpus: graphify's own source, so the KB can answer "how does graphify
# work?" (esp. whether add/write is exposed via MCP or the python API) from the
# graph instead of guessing.
#
# ⚠️ INVARIANT: this pin MUST track the Graphify version the locked uv project installs.
# Otherwise the corpus answers questions about code we are not running. That is
# not hypothetical: until 2026-07-23 this sat at e32c9f43, PREDATING both 0.9.24
# and 0.9.25, while mise ran 0.9.25 — so every "how does graphify work?" answer
# came from the wrong source, and several were wrong.
#
# Pin the RELEASE TAG, never a branch head:
#   - `ref = v8` (the old value) is a BRANCH — it drifts ahead of the release, so
#     the corpus would describe unreleased code.
#   - The newest tag is also wrong: `v1.0.0` is tagged on GitHub but is NOT on
#     PyPI (PyPI latest = 0.9.25, verified 2026-07-23), and mise installs from
#     PyPI — so tracking newest-tag would ingest code we cannot run.
# The correct ref is `v<version>` for the version uv resolves.
#
# ⚠️ FORKED 2026-08-24 (Ray). THE URL BELOW IS NO LONGER UPSTREAM, and the
# invariant above is why it had to move with the pin: `pyproject.toml` now
# installs `graphifyy[all]` from `git+https://github.com/ray-manaloto/graphify@
# <the commit below>`, so leaving this at Graphify-Labs would have put the corpus
# back in
# exactly the 2026-07-23 state described above — describing code we do not run —
# while every surface still LOOKED pinned.
#
# WHY THE FORK, as measured ON 2026-08-24: graphify 0.9.48 had no codex backend,
# and neither did upstream `v8` (byte-identical to v0.9.48 at that moment;
# control-armed — `compare/v0.9.47...v8` reported ahead_by 14, so the endpoint
# discriminates). Both halves are frozen to that date on purpose: `v8` has since
# moved to v0.9.50, so re-read it rather than quoting this. PR #2981 added
# `openai-cli`, a sibling of `claude-cli` that shells to the locally
# authenticated `codex` CLI. It was OPEN and unreviewed when the fork was cut and
# has since been CLOSED WITHOUT MERGING (see the upstream-return note below).
# Ray's call was to take the whole branch rather than cherry-pick, so this pinned
# its head verbatim; the branch has been rebased forward twice since.
#
# THE REF IS A BRANCH WE CREATED, and that contradicts the "never a branch head"
# rule above for one specific reason: the branch recorded in `ref` below — named
# per rebase base, so do not read a version out of this sentence; read it from
# `ref` — in our fork exists ONLY to hold this commit. Nothing pushes to it, so it cannot
# drift the way `v8` does. The `commit` below is still the authority; the branch
# is there so the object survives if TelB-io (whose fork the PR head lives on)
# deletes their branch. Forks share object storage within a network, which is how
# a SHA authored on TelB-io/graphify is reachable here at all.
#
# ⚠️ THE VERSION STRING DOES NOT MOVE WITH THE FORK. It reported `0.9.48` when the
# fork was cut and reports `0.9.50` now — but only because UPSTREAM released twice;
# the fork's own eight commits changed nothing about it. Same name, same version as
# the release it sits on, different code. So version alone cannot tell a forked
# install from an upstream one, which is precisely why `currency.toml`
# `[tool.graphify]` needed a fork-aware state rather than a bumped number.
#
# THE INSTRUMENT THAT CAN TELL, found 2026-08-25: the installed distribution's own
# `direct_url.json` records the commit uv ACTUALLY installed —
#   uv run python -c "from importlib.metadata import distribution; \
#     print(distribution('graphifyy').read_text('direct_url.json'))"
# That is the runtime speaking, where every file below is only a claim about it.
#
# WHAT WOULD RETURN THIS TO UPSTREAM — watch #3073, not #2981.
#
# CORRECTED 2026-09-02. This block said #2981 was closed, concluded upstream was
# "not getting ours", and recorded the fork as PERMANENT rather than a bridge.
# The first clause is true and the conclusion does not follow: #2981 (closed
# 2026-08-25T08:36Z) was RESUPPLIED two days later as **#3073** — same author
# (Azeem1985), byte-identical title, **still OPEN** as of 2026-09-02. A closed PR
# number is not the same fact as an abandoned capability, and reading it that way
# is what made a bridge look permanent. The 2026-08-25 ruling was sound on the
# evidence it had; the evidence moved and nothing re-asked.
#
# ORIGINATION, so it stops being lost (Ray, 2026-09-02): our 8 commits did NOT
# arrive by cherry-picking either PR. They came fork-to-fork from **TelB-io** —
# `origin/kb-pin/openai-cli-backend` carries `Merge pull request #1..#4 from
# TelB-io/feat/*`, and three `# PATCHED FOR TELB-COCKPIT` markers survive in our
# tree (`graphify/llm.py` x2, `graphify/__main__.py` x1). Control-armed: 0 on tag
# v0.9.53, and `openai-cli` in `llm.py` -> 9, so the probe discriminates. Their
# survival IS the proof that commit history plus comments failed to preserve
# where these patches came from.
#
# Upstream v0.9.50 still contained ZERO mentions of `openai-cli` — control-armed
# against 23 mentions of `claude-cli` in the same file, so the zero is an answer
# and not a broken search. What would clear it is upstream shipping an
# openai-cli backend of its own; if that happens, revert `pyproject.toml` to
# `graphifyy[all]==<that version>`, point url/ref/commit here back at
# `Graphify-Labs` at the matching tag, and drop the fork block in currency.toml.
# Upstream ships roughly daily, so re-check rather than assume.
#
# To bump the FORK: rebase the `kb-pin/openai-cli-backend-<base>` branch onto the
# newer upstream tag, push, then set `commit` here and the `@<sha>` in
# `pyproject.toml` together. They are one pin in two files and must move in the
# same commit — and `currency.toml`'s `ref_binding` rows are what find the OTHER
# surfaces carrying the same SHA, which a research lane under-counted 3-to-7 once.
#
# REBASED 2026-08-25 onto upstream v0.9.50. Upstream's DEFAULT branch is `v8`,
# not `main` (`main` has been frozen at 91f4d120 since 2026-05-14, so reading it
# reports a three-month-old tree as "latest"). `v8` HEAD is 43d54acb, which IS
# the `v0.9.50` tag, and `compare/282976b2...43d54acb` reports ahead_by 17 — the
# 17 upstream commits this rebase crossed. Our seven were replayed onto it with
# ONE conflict, in `CHANGELOG.md` only; an eighth commit then fixed the MCP
# disable-override defect that made every openai-cli extraction die in ~3s.
# Re-measure `v8` before assuming this still holds; upstream ships near-daily.
url = https://github.com/ray-manaloto/graphify
ref = kb-pin/openai-cli-backend-v0.9.53
commit = 157a957e89a16246bba3a078de2777711ee85e31
kind = code
added = 2026-07-21
